{"tool_name":"dgsea","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"dgsea","home":"https://jamesjoly.github.io/DGSEA/","summary":"Differential Gene Set Enrichment Analysis (DGSEA) is a R package that provides statistical approach to quantify the relative enrichment of two gene sets.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T09:56:00Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:41:12.402620Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:dgsea","credit":[{"email":"nagraham@usc.edu","name":"Nicholas A Graham","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Differential gene expression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3223"},{"term":"Gene-set enrichment analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2436"},{"term":"Metabolic pathway prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3929"}]}],"name":"DGSEA","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa658","metadata":{"abstract":"Motivation: Gene Set Enrichment Analysis (GSEA) is an algorithm widely used to identify statistically enriched gene sets in transcriptomic data. However, GSEA cannot examine the enrichment of two gene sets or pathways relative to one another. Here we present Differential Gene Set Enrichment Analysis (DGSEA), an adaptation of GSEA that quantifies the relative enrichment of two gene sets. Results: After validating the method using synthetic data, we demonstrate that DGSEA accurately captures the hypoxia-induced coordinated upregulation of glycolysis and downregulation of oxidative phosphorylation. We also show that DGSEA is more predictive than GSEA of the metabolic state of cancer cell lines, including lactate secretion and intracellular concentrations of lactate and AMP. Finally, we demonstrate the application of DGSEA to generate hypotheses about differential metabolic pathway activity in cellular senescence. Together, these data demonstrate that DGSEA is a novel tool to examine the relative enrichment of gene sets in transcriptomic data.","authors":[{"name":"Graham N.A."},{"name":"Joly J.H."},{"name":"Lowry W.E."}],"citationCount":19,"date":"2020-11-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Bioinformatics","title":"Differential Gene Set Enrichment Analysis: A statistical approach to quantify the relative enrichment of two gene sets"},"pmcid":"PMC8453775","pmid":"32692836"}],"topic":[{"term":"Endocrinology and metabolism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3407"},{"term":"Molecular interactions, pathways and networks","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0602"},{"term":"Oncology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2640"},{"term":"RNA-Seq","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3170"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"DGSEA","home":"https://bio.tools/dgsea","summary":"Differential Gene Set Enrichment Analysis (DGSEA) is a R package that provides statistical approach to quantify the relative enrichment of two gene sets.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:dgsea/lib/jamesjoly.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":false,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":22,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2021"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":4,"year":"2022"},{"count":5,"year":"2024"},{"count":5,"year":"2025"},{"count":6,"year":"2023"}],"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btaa658","pmcid":"PMC8453775","pmid":"32692836","ref_count":23,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1997"},{"count":1,"year":"2005"},{"count":1,"year":"2007"},{"count":1,"year":"2009"},{"count":1,"year":"2014"},{"count":3,"yea